// Pull request author: frack113
// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Disabling Windows Defender WMI Autologger Session via Reg.exe
// Sigma ID: ba5a25ce-c969-406c-8510-367541554e95
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Matt Anderson (Huntress)
// Date: 2025-07-09 | Modified: 2026-11-06
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects the use of reg.exe to disable the Event Tracing for Windows (ETW) Autologger session for
//   Windows Defender API and Audit events. By setting the 'Start' value to '0' for the
//   'DefenderApiLogger' or 'DefenderAuditLogger' session, an attacker can prevent these critical
//   security events from being logged, effectively blinding monitoring tools that rely on this data.
//   This is a powerful defense evasion technique.
// False positives:
//   - Highly unlikely
// References:
//   - https://research.splunk.com/endpoint/76406a0f-f5e0-4167-8e1f-337fdc0f1b0c/
//   - https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/etw/configuring-and-starting-an-autologger-session
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2021/10/18/icedid-to-xinglocker-ransomware-in-24-hours/
//   - https://www.threatdown.com/blog/lazyscripter-from-empire-to-double-rat/
//   - https://www.binarly.io/blog/design-issues-of-modern-edrs-bypassing-etw-based-solutions
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ebd26c2d9cd57dc9489faa1f1346577be9947747/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_reg_disable_defender_wmi_autologger.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\reg.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "reg.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Control\\WMI\\Autologger\\DefenderApiLogger\\Start" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Control\\WMI\\Autologger\\DefenderAuditLogger\\Start") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "add" and ProcessCommandLine contains "0")) and (not(ProcessCommandLine contains "0x00000001"))
